# Clinical Agent Safety Rules

## Clinical Agents

| Agent | Purpose | Data Touched |
|-------|---------|-------------|
| CoherenceWorker | Computes C_emo and coherence metrics | Session transcripts, voice biometrics |
| PatternWorker | Detects transgenerational patterns | Session history, family data |
| GrowthEngineWorker | Tracks client growth trajectory | Metrics, session outcomes |
| ForesightWorker | Predictive pattern alerts | Aggregated metrics, session trends |
| RecursiveLearningWorker | AI self-improvement from sessions | Anonymized session data |
| NightSchoolWorker | Wisdom absorption and curriculum | Teaching materials, anonymized cases |
| TherapeuticIntegrityMonitor | Audits AI therapeutic responses | Conversation logs |
| DeadmanSwitch | Client silence monitoring | Last-seen timestamps |

## PII Rules

- **Never log PII** — no names, emails, phone numbers, SSNs, addresses in agent log output
- Use `user_id` (UUID) in logs, never `username` or `name`
- The `PIIDetector` in `night_school_director.py` must run on any data before it enters Night School or Recursive Learning
- Session transcripts processed by agents must be anonymized before storage in teaching tables

## Data Boundaries

Clinical agents **must not**:

- Modify session records directly — they compute metrics and write to metric tables
- Delete any clinical data — only the HEPA Filter (with cooling period) handles deletions
- Share raw session data between clients — ever
- Write clinical data to `skyeye_activity`, `audit_log`, or any non-clinical table
- Expose coherence scores in admin-facing dashboards without aggregation (individual scores are clinical data)

Clinical agents **must**:

- Write to their own metric tables (`coherence_metrics`, `growth_metrics`, `pattern_detections`)
- Respect anonymization thresholds from the coherence engine (Layer 5)
- Use HIPAA-compliant audit trail for any data access

## HIPAA Compliance

All `audit_log` entries from clinical agents must include:

```python
compliance_flags = ['HIPAA']
```

The Nevedal Formula (`C_emo(t)`) and voice biometrics are classified as Protected Health Information (PHI). Any agent that computes or stores these values must:

- Use encrypted connections to the database (enforced by Docker network)
- Never cache PHI in Redis without encryption
- Never include PHI in notification messages (SMS, email, push)

## Deadman Switch Special Rules

The Deadman Switch monitors client silence and alerts coaches:

- Trigger threshold: configurable per client (default 4 hours of silence)
- Notification goes to the **assigned coach**, not the admin
- Never disclose why the alert was triggered in the notification body — just "check in on [client]"
- False positives (client on vacation, different timezone) are acceptable — err on the side of safety
- This agent is HIPAA-critical: silence patterns are clinical data

## Nevedal Formula Protection

The Nevedal Formula is a patented algorithm (Patent Claim #8). Agents that compute it:

- Must use the canonical implementation in `nevedal_engine.py`
- Must not approximate, simplify, or modify the formula
- Must not expose intermediate computation values in logs
- Voice biometric extraction parameters are fixed — do not retune without clinical review
